  "id": "a044d227-5c21-5da6-9daf-2b25ea170559",
  "slug": "multigrain-bagels",
  "name": "Multigrain Bagels",
  "recipe_type": "breakfast",
  "brief_description": "Flaxseed meal, rolled oats, wheat germ, vital wheat gluten, and whole wheat flour add extra fiber, nutrition, and taste to this multigrain bagels recipe.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Combine warm water, yeast, and sugar in a bowl. Let stand until yeast and sugar dissolved and a creamy foam begins to form, about 5 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Combine bread flour, whole wheat flour, rolled oats, vital wheat gluten, wheat germ, flaxseed meal, and sea salt in a large bowl; stir in buttermilk. Add yeast mixture and honey; stir until no dry spots remain. Cover the bowl with plastic wrap; let dough rest 20 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Turn dough out onto a floured surface; knead about 7 minutes, it will be soft and slightly sticky. Add more flour if needed. Shape into a ball. Coat a mixing bowl with cooking spray. Place dough in the bowl and turn to coat. Cover the bowl with plastic wrap; let rise in a warm, draft-free place for 2 hours."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Turn dough onto a floured surface; knead briefly. Cut dough in half; return half to the bowl and cover. Form other half into a cylinder. Cut into quarters and cut quarters in half, yielding 8 equal-sized pieces of dough. Shape dough pieces into balls. Repeat with remaining dough half."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F (200 degrees C). Line one 11x17-inch baking sheet with waxed paper, another baking sheet with a flour sack towel, and two other baking sheets with parchment paper sprinkled with cornmeal."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Combine 3 quarts water and brown sugar in a large pot; bring to a boil."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Meanwhile, flatten 1 dough ball slightly; press index fingers through the center until they meet. Rotate fingers to stretch a hole about 1 \u00be-inch in diameter. Set bagel on waxed paper-lined baking sheet. Repeat with remaining dough balls."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Reduce heat under brown sugar water until simmering. Add 2 bagels at at time to water; boil 30 seconds per side. Transfer boiled bagels to the towel-lined baking sheet to drain, then transfer bagels to the parchment paper-lined baking sheets. Repeat with remaining bagels."
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "text": "Whisk egg white and 1 teaspoon cool water together in a small bowl; brush onto tops of bagels."
    },
    {
      "position": 10,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven for 12 minutes. Flip bagels and continue baking until golden brown, about 13 minutes more."
    },
    {
      "position": 11,
      "text": "Transfer bagels to a wire rack to cool."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 16,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 35,
